 "result_text": "The issue is fixed. The example now serializes to `{'x': {'a': 1}}` and `Bar.from_dict` works too.\n\nThe full suite finished with 25958 passed and 1 failed. The failure is `tests/test_pep_646.py::test_type_name_for_unpacks_py_less_than_311`. It fails the same way with my change stashed, so it was already failing before this fix.\n\nThe cause was `from __future__ import annotations`, which turns annotations into strings. `get_function_arg_annotation` and `get_function_return_annotation` returned them unresolved, so `T` in `dict[str, T]` was never replaced with `int`. Both helpers in `mashumaro/core/meta/helpers.py` now resolve annotations with `get_type_hints` first. If that fails, they fall back to the raw annotation.",
